A process is provided for treating cocoa beans or cocoa nibs, the process including the following operations:

(a) water is combined with the cocoa beans or nibs to produce a suspension;

(b) the resulting suspension is ground while wet;

(c) the suspension is exposed to thermal treatment at a temperature not exceeding 70°C;

(d) the suspension is then divided into three fractions: a water-containing heavy phase, a lighter fat phase that includes cocoa butter, and a solids-containing phase that includes cocoa powder together with liquid constituents;

(e) the liquid constituents are continuously removed from the solids-containing phase produced in step (d), thereby yielding cocoa aroma and cocoa powder, by feeding a stream of that solids-containing phase into a mixing apparatus;

wherein the mixing apparatus includes:

a cylindrical tube-shaped housing positioned along a horizontal axis and provided with an inlet for the solids-containing phase, an outlet for the dried solids-containing phase, and optionally an outlet for a vapor phase containing cocoa aroma;

end plates that seal the tubular housing at both opposing ends;

a coaxial jacket configured to heat or cool the inner wall of the tubular housing to a temperature within the range of 55°C to 150°C; and

a bladed rotor mounted so as to rotate inside the tubular housing, the blades of the rotor being helically arranged and positioned so that they centrifuge the solids-containing phase while at the same time conveying it toward the outlet.

