1. A method of processing cocoa beans or cocoa nibs, the method comprising:

   (a) providing cocoa beans or cocoa nibs as a cocoa starting material;

   (b) wet grinding the cocoa starting material in the presence of an aqueous liquid to form an aqueous cocoa suspension comprising comminuted cocoa solids, cocoa fat, and water-soluble cocoa components;

   (c) subjecting the aqueous cocoa suspension to a low-temperature heat treatment at a temperature below a roasting temperature, thereby reducing microbial load and/or modifying aroma precursor composition while limiting thermal degradation of cocoa aroma components;

   (d) separating the heat-treated aqueous cocoa suspension into at least a fat-rich phase and a solids-containing aqueous phase;

   (e) introducing at least one of the separated phases, or a recombined portion thereof, into a horizontal bladed rotor mixing device comprising a substantially horizontal treatment chamber and a rotor carrying blades configured to mechanically agitate and convey material through the treatment chamber;

   (f) continuously drying the material in the horizontal bladed rotor mixing device by supplying heat to the material while the rotor blades mix, distribute, and advance the material through the treatment chamber, thereby producing a dried cocoa product; and

   (g) recovering aroma compounds released during the continuous drying by withdrawing a vapor stream from the horizontal bladed rotor mixing device and condensing or otherwise collecting at least a portion of the aroma compounds from the vapor stream.

1. A process for treating cocoa nibs to produce cocoa butter, cocoa powder, and cocoa aroma, the process comprising:

providing an apparatus comprising a substantially cylindrical, horizontally disposed mixing vessel having a jacket for thermal conditioning, first and second end plates closing opposed ends of the mixing vessel, at least one inlet opening for introducing cocoa nibs into the mixing vessel, at least one outlet opening for discharging treated cocoa material from the mixing vessel, and a rotor rotatably mounted within the mixing vessel, the rotor comprising a shaft bearing a plurality of helical rotor blades arranged to convey, mix, shear, and agitate cocoa material within the mixing vessel;

introducing cocoa nibs into the mixing vessel through the at least one inlet opening;

rotating the rotor such that the helical rotor blades mechanically work the cocoa nibs while conveying and mixing the cocoa nibs within the mixing vessel;

heating or cooling the mixing vessel by circulating a heat-transfer medium through the jacket to maintain the cocoa nibs at a treatment temperature sufficient to promote release of cocoa butter and volatilization or liberation of cocoa aroma compounds;

recovering a cocoa-aroma-containing vapor or gas stream from the mixing vessel;

discharging, through the at least one outlet opening, a treated cocoa mass comprising cocoa butter and cocoa solids;

separating cocoa butter from the treated cocoa mass; and

processing the remaining cocoa solids to form cocoa powder,

whereby the process produces cocoa butter, cocoa powder, and cocoa aroma from the cocoa nibs.

1. A method for processing cocoa beans, comprising:  
   suspending cocoa beans or cocoa bean material in water to form an aqueous suspension;  
   wet milling the aqueous suspension to reduce particle size of the cocoa bean material;  
   mildly heating the wet-milled aqueous suspension;  
   separating the heated aqueous suspension into at least an aqueous phase, a fat-containing phase, and a cocoa solids phase; and  
   introducing the cocoa solids phase into a heated tubular centrifugal mixer under conditions effective to dry the cocoa solids phase and produce a cocoa powder, while recovering aroma-containing vapors released during drying.

2. The method of claim 1, wherein the mild heating is carried out at a temperature sufficient to facilitate phase separation while limiting thermal degradation of cocoa aroma compounds.

3. The method of claim 1, wherein the fat-containing phase comprises cocoa butter.

4. The method of claim 1, wherein the heated tubular centrifugal mixer imparts centrifugal force and heat transfer to the cocoa solids phase to remove moisture therefrom.

5. The method of claim 1, further comprising condensing or collecting the recovered aroma-containing vapors.

6. The method of claim 5, further comprising adding at least a portion of the recovered aroma-containing vapors, or a condensate thereof, to a cocoa product.

7. The method of claim 1, wherein the cocoa powder has reduced moisture content relative to the cocoa solids phase introduced into the heated tubular centrifugal mixer.

8. A cocoa powder produced by the method of claim 1.

9. A system for processing cocoa beans, comprising:  
   a vessel configured to suspend cocoa beans or cocoa bean material in water;  
   a wet mill configured to mill the aqueous suspension;  
   a heater configured to mildly heat the milled aqueous suspension;  
   a separator configured to separate the heated aqueous suspension into an aqueous phase, a fat-containing phase, and a cocoa solids phase; and  
   a heated tubular centrifugal mixer configured to receive the cocoa solids phase, dry the cocoa solids phase to form cocoa powder, and discharge aroma-containing vapors for recovery.
